  {
    "id": "1788987757140",
    "name": "Maison Pickle",
    "category": "dining",
    "day": "",
    "address": "Maison Pickle, 2315 Broadway, New York, NY 10024, United States",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nLocated squarely on the vibrant Upper West Side, this upscale American eatery is anchored beautifully at 2322 Broadway, sitting proudly between 84th and 85th Streets.\n\nThe Jacob’s Pedigree\nThis magnificent establishment is the highly acclaimed, sophisticated sister restaurant to the legendary Jacob’s Pickles, elevating classic American comfort food with a stunning, French-inspired culinary twist.\n\nThe French Dip Architecture\nYou absolutely must order their signature French Dip. The culinary team masterfully stacks mountains of incredibly tender, slow-roasted beef on artisanal French bread, served alongside a brilliant, deeply savory cup of hot au jus.\n\nThe Gruyère Crown\nElevate the classic sandwich by ordering the Deluxe version. It features a flawless, bubbling crown of rich, heavily melted Gruyère cheese and deeply caramelized onions baked directly onto the hot crust.\n\nThe Brioche Masterpiece\nDo not skip the appetizers. Their legendary pull-apart bread is a towering, beautifully baked brioche masterpiece, glistening with rich garlic butter and meant to be aggressively torn apart by hand.\n\nThe Culinary Weight\nThese massive, richly layered sandwiches carry a dense, deeply satisfying payload. They are perfectly engineered to effortlessly fuel a massive day of exploring the expansive museums and historic streets of the surrounding neighborhood.\n\nThe Shared Tasting\nBecause the portions are gloriously monumental, beautifully split a French Dip and an order of the rich pull-apart bread with a travel companion to sample the absolute best of the menu in a single visit without feeling weighed down.\n\nThe Vintage Aesthetic\nStep inside and admire the stunning, meticulously designed interior. It features soaring ceilings, deeply tufted green leather booths, and warm, glowing vintage chandeliers that evoke the timeless elegance of classic New York dining.\n\nThe Bar Architecture\nThe massive, sweeping bar is an absolute design triumph. Backlit shelves brilliantly showcase an incredible library of premium spirits, framed perfectly by classic subway tiles and highly polished dark wood accents.\n\nThe Cocktail Presentation\nThe mixology program here is an absolute masterclass. Their signature cocktails are presented in stunning, heavy-bottomed crystal glassware, brilliantly garnished with fresh herbs and large, perfectly clear artisanal ice cubes.\n\nThe Macro Perspective\nBefore taking your first bite, activate your camera's dedicated macro mode. Get incredibly close to the French Dip to beautifully capture the glistening, savory juices of the slow-roasted beef and the heavy, shining cheese pull.\n\nThe Au Jus Action\nFor a brilliant, cinematic food video, use a slow-motion frame rate to flawlessly capture the heavy, rich au jus cascading directly over the toasted bread and tender beef as you dunk the sandwich.\n\nThe Tungsten Glow\nThe restaurant is bathed in beautifully warm, low-level tungsten lighting. Lean into this classic, moody atmosphere by resting your camera on the table to capture the brilliant reflections off the crystal glassware without ever using a harsh flash.\n\nThe Central Park Pivot\nOnce you finish your incredibly satisfying meal, take a scenic walk to burn off the rich food. Head exactly three blocks east to seamlessly transition into the sweeping, beautifully landscaped, historic paths of Central Park.\n\nThe Subway Approach\nTransit is incredibly effortless. Take the 1 train directly to the 86th Street station. Emerge from the underground and enjoy a beautiful, incredibly short two-block walk south down the vibrant Broadway corridor to hit the stunning storefront.",
    "summary": "Maison Pickle is known for comforting American classics, especially hearty French Dip sandwiches, fried chicken, burgers, and indulgent sides.",
    "image": "images/125.jpg",
    "cost": null,
    "packageId": null,
    "website": "https://www.maisonpickle.com",
    "lat": 40.7870846,
    "lng": -73.9771627,
    "rating": null
  },
  {
    "id": "1788987911764",
    "name": "Tony’s Di Napoli",
    "category": "dining",
    "day": "",
    "address": "Tony's Di Napoli, 147 W 43rd St, New York, NY 10036, United States",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly. This iconic, bustling cathedral of Italian-American dining is anchored beautifully at 147 West 43rd Street, sitting perfectly in the vibrant, glowing heart of the Theater District.\n\nThe Family-Style Architecture\nDo not expect standard, individual plates. The entire menu is brilliantly engineered around massive, family-style platters designed to perfectly recreate the generous, grand scale of a traditional New York Sunday supper.\n\nThe Chicken Parmigiana\nYou absolutely must order their signature Chicken Parmigiana. The culinary team masterfully bakes a towering, crispy cutlet beneath a flawless, bubbling crown of rich mozzarella and a sweet, deeply savory marinara sauce.\n\nThe Shared Tasting\nBecause the portions are gloriously monumental, beautifully split a main course and a massive bowl of classic rigatoni alla vodka with a travel companion to seamlessly sample the absolute best of the menu in a single visit.\n\nThe Broadway Gallery\nStep inside and admire the stunning, meticulously curated interior. The walls are completely covered in hundreds of beautiful, framed caricatures and portraits of legendary Broadway stars and celebrities who frequent the dining room.\n\nThe Theatrical Energy\nVisit during the peak 6:30 PM pre-theater rush to witness a masterclass in urban dining. The incredibly fast, beautifully choreographed speed of the waitstaff maneuvering massive platters through the packed room is a brilliant display of city energy.\n\nThe Garlic Bread Foundation\nDo not ignore the complimentary bread basket. It is a towering, beautifully baked masterpiece of fresh Italian bread, arriving warm to the table and setting a flawless, savory foundation to soak up the rich pasta sauces to come.\n\nThe Tableside Theater\nWatch the expert waitstaff carefully. They perform a brilliant, rhythmic culinary theater, expertly transferring the towering mountains of pasta and rich meats from the central serving platter directly to your individual plates with absolute precision.\n\nThe Culinary Weight\nThese massive, richly layered Italian dishes carry a dense, deeply satisfying payload. They are perfectly engineered to effortlessly fuel a massive evening of exploring the soaring skyscrapers and endless entertainment of the surrounding Midtown canyons.\n\nThe Dessert Monument\nYou must save room for the finale. Their signature dessert is a towering, flawlessly constructed strawberry shortcake, built with incredibly fluffy sponge, mountains of fresh whipped cream, and vibrantly sweet, brilliantly red berries.\n\nThe Macro Detail\nBefore taking your first bite, activate your camera's dedicated macro mode. Get incredibly close to the Chicken Parmigiana to beautifully capture the glistening, savory marinara and the heavy, shining cheese pull as the mozzarella stretches.\n\nThe Action Shot\nFor a brilliant, cinematic food video, use a slow-motion frame rate to flawlessly capture the waitstaff lifting a massive, steaming forkful of linguine from the main platter, perfectly highlighting the incredible, generous scale of the dish.\n\nThe Tungsten Glow\nThe bustling dining room is bathed in beautifully warm, classic New York tungsten lighting. Lean into this nostalgic, grand atmosphere by framing your food against the glowing chandeliers and the iconic, deeply colored artwork on the walls.\n\nThe Times Square Pivot\nOnce you finish your incredibly satisfying meal, you are standing directly in the center of global entertainment. Walk exactly half a block west to seamlessly transition into the sweeping, brilliantly illuminated neon canyons of Times Square.\n\nThe Subway Approach\nTransit is incredibly effortless. Take the 1, 2, 3, N, Q, R, or W train directly to the massive Times Square–42nd Street station. Emerge from the underground and enjoy a beautiful, incredibly short walk through the vibrant theater crowds to hit the awning.",
    "summary": "Tony’s Di Napoli is known for family-style Italian dining, with generous portions of pasta, seafood, chicken, veal, and classic red-sauce dishes.",
    "image": "images/126.jpg",
    "cost": null,
    "packageId": null,
    "website": "https://www.tonysnyc.com/",
    "lat": 40.756498,
    "lng": -73.985397,
    "rating": null,
    "locations": [
      {
        "address": "Tony's Di Napoli, 1081 3rd Ave, New York, NY 10065, United States",
        "lat": 40.7643725,
        "lng": -73.9642919
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "1788988145233",
    "name": "Carmine’s – Times Square",
