    "address": "Carmine's - 44th Street - NYC, 200 W 44th St, New York, NY 10036, United States",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly. This legendary, roaring cathedral of Southern Italian dining is anchored beautifully at 200 West 44th Street, sitting precisely in the vibrant, glowing epicenter of the Theater District.\n\nThe 1940s Aesthetic\nStep inside and admire the stunning, meticulously designed interior. The soaring ceilings, dark polished woods, and warm vintage chandeliers perfectly recreate the grand, nostalgic atmosphere of a classic 1940s New York supper club.\n\nThe Family-Style Architecture\nDo not expect standard, individual plates. The entire culinary program is brilliantly engineered around massive, monumental platters designed to perfectly replicate a traditional, incredibly generous Italian-American Sunday feast.\n\nThe Meatball Monument\nYou absolutely must order the classic spaghetti and meatballs. The culinary team masterfully crafts towering, incredibly dense meatballs that arrive completely blanketed in a rich, flawless, deeply savory house marinara.\n\nThe Chicken Scarpariello\nIf you want to look beyond the classic Parmigiana, this dish is an absolute masterpiece. It features perfectly roasted chicken on the bone, beautifully tossed with bright lemon, fresh rosemary, and heavily caramelized garlic.\n\nThe Shared Tasting\nBecause the portions are gloriously colossal, beautifully split a massive platter of pasta and a towering salad with a travel companion. This allows you to seamlessly sample the absolute best of the menu in a single visit without ordering excess.\n\nThe Theatrical Energy\nVisit during the peak 5:30 PM pre-theater rush to witness an absolute masterclass in urban dining. The incredibly fast, beautifully choreographed speed of the waitstaff maneuvering massive, steaming platters through the packed room is a brilliant display of city energy.\n\nThe Garlic Bread Foundation\nDo not ignore the complimentary bread basket. It arrives to the table as a towering, beautifully baked foundation of fresh, warm Italian bread, perfectly engineered to soak up the rich, vibrant pasta sauces left on your plate.\n\nThe Culinary Weight\nThese massive, richly layered Italian dishes carry a dense, deeply satisfying payload. They are perfectly designed to effortlessly fuel a massive evening of exploring the soaring skyscrapers and endless entertainment of the surrounding Midtown canyons.\n\nThe Titanic Finale\nYou must save room for their legendary dessert. The Titanic is a towering, flawlessly constructed architectural marvel built with a massive chocolate torte, mountains of premium ice cream, and cascades of fresh whipped cream and hot fudge.\n\nThe Tableside Theater\nWatch the expert waitstaff carefully. They perform a brilliant, rhythmic culinary theater, expertly transferring the towering mountains of pasta and rich meats from the central serving platter directly to your individual plates with absolute precision.\n\nThe Macro Detail\nBefore taking your first bite, activate your smartphone's dedicated macro mode. Get incredibly close to the towering pasta platters to beautifully capture the glistening, savory marinara and the brilliant, textured grate of fresh Romano cheese.\n\nThe Action Shot\nFor a brilliant, cinematic food video, use a slow-motion frame rate to flawlessly capture the waitstaff lifting a massive, steaming forkful of linguine directly from the main platter, perfectly highlighting the incredible, generous scale of the dish.\n\nThe Times Square Pivot\nOnce you finish your incredibly satisfying meal, you are standing directly in the center of global entertainment. Walk exactly a few steps east to seamlessly transition into the sweeping, brilliantly illuminated neon canyons of Times Square.\n\nThe Subway Approach\nTransit is incredibly effortless. Take the 1, 2, 3, N, Q, R, or W train directly to the massive Times Square–42nd Street station. Emerge from the underground and enjoy a beautiful, incredibly short walk through the vibrant theater crowds to hit the iconic awning.",
    "summary": "Carmine’s is a classic Italian-American restaurant known for generous family-style portions, hearty pasta, seafood, meat dishes, and desserts.",
