  {
    "id": "1788988381088",
    "name": "Texas Roadhouse",
    "category": "dining",
    "day": "",
    "address": "Texas Roadhouse, 2571 Hempstead Tpke Ste 100, East Meadow, NY 11554, United States",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly. This bustling steakhouse sits at 2571 Hempstead Turnpike in East Meadow, Nassau County, on a busy commercial stretch of Long Island rather than anywhere in the five boroughs.\n\nThe Architectural Scale\nThis is not a cramped Manhattan dining room. The building is a massive, sprawling, brilliantly constructed wooden lodge featuring soaring ceilings, bright neon accents, and a classic footprint that perfectly captures the expansive spirit of the American West.\n\nThe Meat Display\nStep inside the front doors and admire the stunning, brightly lit glass meat cooler. The culinary team meticulously displays the hand-cut, brilliantly marbled steaks like precious artifacts, perfectly showcasing the incredible quality of the beef before it hits the roaring grill.\n\nThe Cinnamon Butter Foundation\nDo not ignore the complimentary bread basket. It arrives to the table as a towering, beautifully baked foundation of fresh, warm yeast rolls, served alongside a flawless, deeply sweet, and perfectly whipped cinnamon butter.\n\nThe Bone-In Ribeye\nYou absolutely must order their signature bone-in ribeye. The culinary team masterfully sears this massive, beautifully marbled cut over an open flame to create a flawless, caramelized crust while locking in the rich, deeply savory juices.\n\nThe Cactus Blossom\nThe appetizers are absolute architectural marvels. The legendary Cactus Blossom is a towering, flawlessly deep-fried colossus of a sweet onion, brilliantly engineered to pull apart into perfect, golden, crispy petals ready for dunking in their rich, signature sauce.\n\nThe Shared Tasting\nBecause the portions are gloriously colossal, beautifully split a massive steak and a towering mountain of loaded potato skins with a travel companion. This allows you to seamlessly sample the absolute best of the menu in a single visit without ordering excess.\n\nThe Line Dancing Theater\nVisit during the peak dinner rush to witness a masterclass in dining entertainment. The incredibly energetic, beautifully choreographed speed of the waitstaff breaking into spontaneous line dances is a brilliant, highly spirited display of unique restaurant culture.\n\nThe Peanut Tradition\nEmbrace the absolute classic, nostalgic energy of the dining room. The experience is beautifully defined by the legendary buckets of complimentary roasted peanuts on the tables, creating an incredibly relaxed, welcoming, and uniquely interactive atmosphere.\n\nThe Culinary Weight\nThese massive, richly layered American dishes carry a dense, deeply satisfying payload. They are perfectly designed to fuel an evening out on Long Island.\n\nThe Ice-Cold Tap\nThe beverage program is an absolute triumph of temperature control. Their signature draft beers and margaritas are served in brilliantly frosted, heavy glass mugs, ensuring a flawless, refreshing, ice-cold sip that perfectly cuts through the rich, savory steaks.\n\nThe Macro Detail\nBefore taking your first bite, activate your camera's dedicated macro mode. Get incredibly close to the towering ribeye to beautifully capture the glistening, savory juices, the perfect crosshatch grill marks, and the melting pat of seasoned butter.\n\nThe Action Shot\nFor a brilliant, cinematic food video, use a slow-motion frame rate to flawlessly capture the waitstaff setting down the massive, steaming plates, perfectly highlighting the incredible, generous scale of the beautifully plated meal.\n\nThe Eisenhower Park Pivot\nOnce you finish your meal, a short drive away is Eisenhower Park, one of Nassau County's largest parks, with wide walking paths for working off the steak.\n\nThe Driving Approach\nLong Island is car-country: driving is by far the easiest way to reach this restaurant. If you are coming from Manhattan, take the LIRR to a Nassau County station such as Hempstead, then use a rideshare or taxi. Check current NICE bus routes along Hempstead Turnpike before relying on one.",
    "summary": "Texas Roadhouse is known for hand-cut steaks, fall-off-the-bone ribs, fresh-baked bread, and hearty made-from-scratch sides.",
    "image": "images/128.jpg",
    "cost": null,
    "packageId": null,
    "website": "https://www.texasroadhouse.com",
    "lat": 40.725085,
    "lng": -73.5404517,
    "rating": null
  },
  {
    "id": "1788988581900",
    "name": "Westlight",
    "category": "dining",
    "day": "",
    "address": "Westlight, 111 N 12th St, Brooklyn, NY 11249, United States",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly around the dense Williamsburg grid. This massively celebrated, highly elevated cocktail sanctuary is brilliantly anchored at 111 North 12th Street, sitting directly on the 22nd floor of The William Vale.\n\nThe Free Viewpoint Hack\nEmbrace the massive value of this world-class architectural elevation. You can flawlessly access the sprawling outdoor wraparound terrace to capture completely complimentary panoramic photographs of the skyline without officially sitting for a heavily priced table service.\n\nThe Reservation Protocol\nExecute absolute precision when planning your evening. Because this venue commands massive global popularity, you must flawlessly secure a digital reservation weeks in advance to completely bypass the incredibly chaotic standby line.\n\nThe Sunset Strategy\nPlan your visit perfectly for the late afternoon transition to secure the absolute best visual experience. Watching the warm, heavy sunlight brilliantly drop behind the towering Manhattan skyline creates a deeply cinematic, highly dramatic atmosphere.\n\nThe Wind Chill Reality\nAlways pack a light outer layer in your day bag before heading into the sky. The heavy, high-speed winds ripping directly off the East River at this massive elevation can instantly drop the perceived temperature the second you step onto the terrace.\n\nThe Glass Box Sanctuary\nIf the brutal waterfront weather becomes completely overwhelming, seek immediate refuge indoors. The brilliant designers flawlessly encased the massive main bar in floor-to-ceiling glass, completely shielding you while maintaining the sweeping views.\n\nThe Signature Cocktail\nElevate your heavy evening by securing a highly engineered beverage from the bustling bar. The expert mixologists brilliantly utilize deeply rich, premium spirits to create incredibly complex, highly refreshing signature cocktails that flawlessly match the luxury aesthetic.\n\nThe Tempura Crunch\nBalance the heavy alcohol intake by commanding an order of their highly celebrated rock shrimp tempura. The kitchen flawlessly executes a beautifully crispy, deeply savory batter that perfectly contrasts with the rich cocktail profiles.\n\nThe Binocular Integration\nDo not ignore the highly strategic optical equipment mounted directly to the massive glass railings. You can flawlessly utilize these classic viewing towers to heavily magnify the deeply intricate architectural details of Midtown Manhattan across the water.\n\nThe Dress Code Enforcement\nExecute absolute precision when selecting your outfit for this highly elevated experience. The strict door staff flawlessly enforces a polished, upscale casual dress code, meaning you must completely abandon heavy athletic wear to secure entry.\n\nThe High-Speed Ascent\nPrepare for a highly kinetic, deeply immersive transit experience before even reaching the bar. The brilliantly engineered express elevators flawlessly launch you twenty-two stories into the sky at massive speeds, completely bypassing the lower hotel floors.\n\nThe Wide-Angle Capture\nSwitch your smartphone camera to its dedicated 0.5x ultra-wide lens exactly when you step onto the open deck. A sweeping shot flawlessly frames the massive glass barriers, the rushing East River, and the sprawling concrete grid in one brilliant image.\n\nThe Silhouette Portrait\nFor a brilliant, highly stylized social media image, position your subject directly against the heavy glass railing just after sundown. Flawlessly capture their dark silhouette contrasted heavily against the brightly glowing city lights in the distance.\n\nThe Late-Night Shift\nAppreciate the incredibly dynamic, shifting energy of the massive room. As the evening progresses, the deeply relaxed sunset lounge flawlessly transitions into a highly kinetic, heavy-bass nightlife destination dominated by local Brooklyn crowds.\n\nThe Transit Approach\nNavigating to this towering sanctuary requires a highly strategic subway drop-off. Ride the L train directly to the bustling Bedford Avenue station, emerging from the underground for a brisk, highly scenic ten-minute stroll straight toward the hotel.",
    "summary": "A sprawling, highly cinematic rooftop bar crowning the 22nd floor of The William Vale, offering massive panoramic views of the Manhattan skyline.",
