  {
    "id": "1789065190867",
    "name": "The Monster Crab",
    "category": "dining",
    "day": "",
    "address": "The Monster Crab AYCE Seafood & Bar, 242 Voice Rd, Carle Place, NY 11514, United States",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly. This Cajun-style seafood spot is at 242 Voice Road in Carle Place, Nassau County, on Long Island.\n\nThe Nautical Aesthetic\nStep inside and admire the stunning, meticulously designed interior. The dining room features soaring ceilings, heavily distressed maritime wood, and glowing, classic nautical fixtures that brilliantly recreate the energy of a bustling coastal wharf.\n\nThe Bag Architecture\nDo not expect standard, flat plates. The main event arrives directly to the table in massive, heavy-duty, translucent steam bags—a flawless, highly engineered presentation method designed completely to lock in roaring heat and deeply infuse the rich spices.\n\nThe Seafood Colossus\nThe absolute star of the menu is the massive, customizable boil. Expect towering, flawlessly steamed clusters of premium snow crab legs, colossal shrimp, and thick, sweet lobster tails all resting in a glorious sea of rich flavor.\n\nThe Signature Spice\nYou absolutely must order the house-special seasoning blend. It is an absolute culinary triumph, brilliantly merging deeply savory, heavily caramelized garlic butter with a vibrant, flawlessly calibrated Cajun heat.\n\nThe Tactile Theater\nEmbrace the brilliant, interactive dining architecture. The establishment completely dispenses with formal cutlery, encouraging a flawlessly hands-on, highly energetic experience equipped perfectly with thick, custom bibs and heavy steel shell crackers.\n\nThe Vegetable Foundation\nDo not ignore the brilliant accompaniments. The bottom of every massive steam bag contains a beautiful, savory foundation of sweet corn on the cob and tender red potatoes, engineered perfectly to absorb the massive, rich pools of spiced butter.\n\nThe Deep-Fried Mastery\nIf you want to look beyond the boils, the kitchen executes an absolute masterclass in golden, heavy frying. The perfectly breaded, brilliantly crispy soft-shell crab and catfish baskets deliver a flawless, crackling crunch that perfectly complements the steamed shellfish.\n\nThe Shared Tasting\nBecause the portions are gloriously colossal, beautifully split a massive grand combination bag with a travel companion. This allows for a seamless, perfectly balanced sampling of the absolute best of the ocean in a single, towering order.\n\nThe Culinary Weight\nThese massive, richly layered seafood feasts carry a dense, deeply satisfying payload. They are perfectly engineered to fuel an evening of exploring the surrounding Nassau County area.\n\nThe Steam Plume\nWatch the table presentation carefully. When the server finally unties the heavy bag, it releases a towering, brilliant plume of intensely fragrant, heavily spiced steam—a completely flawless, aromatic moment of dining theater.\n\nThe Action Shot\nFor a brilliant, cinematic food video, use a slow-motion frame rate to flawlessly capture the exact moment the massive crab legs are cracked open, perfectly highlighting the incredible, delicate white meat sliding effortlessly from the vibrant red shell.\n\nThe Macro Detail\nBefore consuming the masterpiece, activate the camera's dedicated macro mode. Get incredibly close to the towering seafood to beautifully capture the glistening, deeply savory pools of garlic butter completely coating the pristine shellfish.\n\nThe Roosevelt Field Pivot\nOnce you finish the meal, the big retail complex of Roosevelt Field in nearby Garden City is a short drive away if you want to walk off the boil among the shops.\n\nThe Transit Approach\nCarle Place has its own LIRR station, so a train from Penn Station followed by a short taxi or rideshare is workable. Driving is easier if you have a car; check the map for the exact distance from the station.",
    "summary": "The Monster Crab serves Cajun-style seafood boils featuring crab, shrimp, lobster, crawfish, and flavorful sauces.",
    "image": "images/132.jpg",
    "cost": null,
    "packageId": null,
    "website": "https://themonstercrab.com",
    "lat": 40.7463493,
    "lng": -73.6197067,
    "rating": null,
    "locations": [
