    "address": "Cinnabar, 45 Carmans Rd, Massapequa, NY 11758, United States",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly. This monumental, highly acclaimed cathedral of Asian fusion and traditional Chinese cuisine is anchored beautifully at 45 Carmans Road, sitting perfectly within the vibrant, expansive corridors of Massapequa on Long Island.\n\nThe Architectural Scale\nStep inside and admire the stunning, meticulously designed interior. The dining room features soaring ceilings, brilliant glowing lanterns, and deeply polished dark woods that perfectly recreate the grand, nostalgic atmosphere of a classic, upscale banquet hall.\n\nThe Peking Duck Theater\nYou absolutely must order the signature Peking Duck. The master chefs perform a brilliant, continuous culinary theater, meticulously carving the heavily caramelized, flawlessly roasted bird directly at the table with absolute precision.\n\nThe Dim Sum Baskets\nDo not ignore the towering bamboo baskets. The kitchen meticulously maintains a roaring, continuous steam cycle, presenting beautifully delicate har gow and perfectly fluffy, warm bao buns that deliver a flawless, traditional savory bite.\n\nThe Wok Mastery\nWatch the open kitchen carefully to witness an absolute masterclass in heat control. The chefs expertly toss massive woks over roaring, brilliant open flames, creating the deeply savory, irreplaceable flavor profile known as wok hei.\n\nThe Sushi Gallery\nStep up to the beautifully illuminated sushi bar. The chefs perform a brilliant culinary dance, meticulously rolling fresh, jewel-toned maki and slicing delicate, brilliantly colored sashimi to perfectly balance the hot, savory dishes.\n\nThe Seafood Colossus\nThe live seafood program is a stunning tribute to the ocean. Expect towering, flawlessly steamed platters of premium lobster and colossal shrimp, all resting in a glorious pool of rich, deeply aromatic ginger and scallion sauce.\n\nThe Tea Foundation\nDo not settle for standard tap water. The meal is beautifully anchored by a continuous, flowing supply of premium, highly aromatic jasmine tea, served from classic ceramic pots to flawlessly cleanse the palate between rich courses.\n\nThe Shared Tasting\nBecause the portions are gloriously colossal, beautifully split a massive platter of crispy beef and a towering mountain of lo mein with a travel companion. This allows for a seamless, perfectly balanced sampling of the absolute best of the menu in a single visit.\n\nThe Culinary Weight\nThese massive, richly layered dishes carry a dense, deeply satisfying payload. They are perfectly engineered to effortlessly fuel a massive evening of exploring the expansive, historic shorelines and sprawling retail avenues of Long Island.\n\nThe Cocktail Program\nThe massive, sweeping bar is an absolute design triumph. Backlit shelves brilliantly showcase an incredible library of premium spirits, allowing the mixologists to craft stunning, brilliantly garnished cocktails served in heavy-bottomed crystal glassware.\n\nThe Golden Hour Glow\nThe bustling dining room is bathed in beautifully warm, ambient lighting. Lean into this classic, grand atmosphere by framing your food against the glowing, intricately carved wooden dividers to capture a beautiful, cinematic glow.\n\nThe Macro Detail\nBefore taking the first bite, activate the camera's dedicated macro mode. Get incredibly close to the towering plates to beautifully capture the glistening, deeply caramelized crust of the roasted duck and the brilliant, translucent folds of the dumplings.\n\nThe Nature Preserve Pivot\nOnce you finish the incredibly satisfying meal, take a beautiful, scenic trip to burn off the energy. Head seamlessly toward the sweeping, meticulously landscaped botanical pathways and tranquil lakes of the nearby Massapequa Preserve.\n\nThe Transit Approach\nTransit is an incredible, highly scenic journey. Take the iconic, absolutely beautiful Long Island Rail Road (LIRR) directly to the Massapequa station. Emerge from the platform and enjoy a seamless, brilliantly efficient connection to this sprawling culinary destination.",
    "summary": "Cinnabar serves Japanese and Chinese cuisine, including sushi, sashimi, seafood boils, dim sum, and creative specialty dishes.",
