  {
    "id": "1794675946260",
    "name": "UMI Hotpot Sushi & Seafood Buffet",
    "category": "dining",
    "day": "",
    "website": "https://www.umibuffet.com/",
    "address": "Umi Sushi & Seafood Buffet, 220-18 Hillside Ave., Queens Village, NY 11427, United States",
    "summary": "A massive, all-you-can-eat feast featuring individual hotpots, fresh sashimi, snow crab legs, and endless dim sum in an upscale setting.",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly when an epic, high-volume seafood craving strikes. This massive, dazzling culinary palace is prominently anchored along a bustling commercial corridor with expansive parking and immediate highway access.\n\nThe Grand Buffet Scale\nStep inside a sprawling, modern dining arena engineered for maximum gastronomic variety. Illuminated display stations stretch across the room, housing hundreds of chilled seafood delicacies, artisanal sushi rolls, and sizzling hot entrees.\n\nThe Individual Hotpot Setup\nForget sharing a single communal pot and compromising on spice levels. Every seat at the table is equipped with its own dedicated induction burner, allowing each diner to command a personalized simmering broth from start to finish.\n\nThe Broth Foundation\nStart the culinary journey by selecting a richly flavored soup base from the digital ordering system. The fiery Sichuan mala tallow broth delivers an authentic numbing heat, while the slow-simmered pork bone and mushroom broths offer deep, savory comfort.\n\nThe Snow Crab Strategy\nHead straight for the towering mountains of chilled snow crab legs and jumbo shrimp on the first pass. Securing a generous plate of sweet, crack-ready crustaceans immediately sets an indulgent tone before the hotpot broth even reaches a rolling boil.\n\nThe Sashimi Precision\nBypass the heavy rice-filled rolls early on to maximize appetite for the raw bar. Expertly sliced salmon, tuna, and yellowtail sashimi are continuously replenished on crushed ice, offering buttery textures that rival standalone sushi counters.\n\nThe Custom Sauce Lab\nVisit the sprawling condiment bar to engineer a signature dipping sauce before cooking begins. Whisk together rich sesame paste, pungent minced garlic, fresh cilantro, scallions, chili oil, and a splash of black vinegar for the ultimate flavor amplifier.\n\nThe Wagyu & Lamb Plunge\nSwirl paper-thin ribbons of marbled beef and tender lamb shoulder through the boiling broth for just a few seconds. Removing the meat the exact moment it turns opaque preserves its melt-in-your-mouth tenderness and locks in the rich broth aromatics.\n\nThe Two-Hour Pacing\nThe all-you-can-eat experience operates on a strict two-hour dining window to keep the bustling waitlists moving smoothly. Pace the courses strategically by alternating between rich boiled meats, crisp chilled shellfish, and refreshing citrus palate cleansers.\n\nThe Dim Sum & Grill Station\nSave room to explore the steaming bamboo baskets and sizzling teppanyaki grill counters. Freshly steamed shrimp shumai, roast Peking duck, and charred beef short ribs provide a savory, smoky contrast to the simmering hotpot ingredients.\n\nThe Neon & Marble Aesthetic\nAdmire the sleek, contemporary interior design featuring glowing neon accents, polished stone tabletops, and dramatic chandelier lighting. The upscale, energetic atmosphere transforms a casual buffet meal into a vibrant celebratory night out.\n\nThe Steam & Action Shot\nCapture a dynamic, cinematic video clip right at the table as the induction burner hits peak intensity. Frame the shot closely as ribbons of marbled beef dip into the bubbling crimson chili broth through a rising cloud of aromatic steam.\n\nThe Shellfish Flat-Lay\nBefore diving into the first course, arrange a colorful platter of vibrant orange snow crab, ruby-red tuna sashimi, and emerald seaweed salad. Shoot directly from overhead in 0.5x or 1x mode to capture the sheer scale and vibrant contrast of the feast.\n\nThe Sweet Finale\nConclude the marathon meal at the dedicated dessert bar stocked with French macarons, tiramisu, and soft-serve ice cream. Pairing warm, crispy brown sugar mochi or fresh tropical fruit with green tea ice cream cuts through the rich, savory spice.\n\nThe Peak Hour Timing\nArrive thirty minutes before the standard dinner rush or book ahead for large groups, as weekend evenings draw massive crowds. Transitioning from lunch to dinner pricing occurs mid-afternoon, when the kitchen brings out the premium crab and sashimi selections.",
