  {
    "id": "1794676695472",
    "name": "The Roof at PUBLIC Hotel",
    "category": "dining",
    "day": "",
    "website": "https://www.publichotels.com/newyork/eat-and-drink/the-roof",
    "address": "THE ROOF, 215 Chrystie St, New York, NY 10002, United States",
    "summary": "A sleek 18th-floor rooftop lounge and lush outdoor terrace offering 360-degree Manhattan skyline views, craft cocktails, and late-night DJs.",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly down the Lower East Side blocks searching for the entrance. This iconic sky-high sanctuary crowns the 18th floor of the sleek PUBLIC Hotel, anchored directly at 215 Chrystie Street just below Houston Street.\n\nThe Dedicated Entrance\nBypass the main hotel check-in lobby if you are heading straight up for evening drinks. Look directly to the left of the main hotel entrance on Chrystie Street to find the dedicated rooftop queue and express elevator access.\n\nThe Neon Escalator Prelude\nIf entering through the main hotel atrium earlier in the day, take a moment to admire the architectural drama. The famous glowing, mirror-lined neon escalators ascending from the street level provide one of the most futuristic entryways in Manhattan.\n\nThe 360-Degree Panorama\nStep out onto the landscaped wrap-around terrace for an unobstructed visual sweep of the entire island. Because the surrounding Lower East Side buildings sit relatively low, the terrace delivers a rare, jaw-dropping view stretching from One World Trade to the Empire State Building.\n\nThe Sunset Happy Hour\nPlan to arrive between 5:00 PM and 7:00 PM from Monday through Friday to experience the golden-hour transformation. Arriving in this early window guarantees relaxed terrace seating, shorter elevator waits, and sunset specials before the late-night velvet rope tightens.\n\nThe Dual Atmosphere\nThis venue effortlessly shifts its identity as the sun dips below the Hudson River. Early evenings feel like a lush, floating botanical garden for quiet conversation, while post-10:00 PM transforms the glassed-in lounge into a high-energy dancefloor in the sky.\n\nThe Smart Casual Code\nDoorman discretion is strictly enforced once the evening nightlife shift begins. Leave athletic wear, sweatpants, flip-flops, and casual gym sneakers behind in favor of sharp, smart-casual attire to breeze past the street-level podium.\n\nThe Craft Cocktail Lineup\nOrder a signature botanical or spicy agave creation from the central wrap-around bar. The mixology program leans heavily into bright, refreshing flavor profiles designed to pair effortlessly with warm sunset breezes and skyline gazing.\n\nThe Glassed-In Sanctuary\nDo not let a sudden chill or passing rain shower derail your rooftop plans. The interior lounge is completely encased in floor-to-ceiling panoramic glass, ensuring uninterrupted views of the glittering skyscrapers from a climate-controlled booth.\n\nThe Golden Hour Framing\nPosition yourself along the western edge of the outdoor terrace thirty minutes before sundown. Frame your portrait shots with the glass parapet in the foreground and the glowing Midtown towers catching the warm amber light in the distance.\n\nThe Nighttime Bokeh Shot\nOnce darkness falls and the city grid ignites, switch your camera to night mode or a wide aperture. Capture a dramatic, high-contrast silhouette against the sea of illuminated skyscraper windows without using a harsh camera flash.\n\nThe Reservation Strategy\nBook a table in advance via Resy or the official hotel portal if visiting with a group on a Thursday, Friday, or Saturday night. Having a confirmed booking bypasses the general walk-in queue and secures prime indoor-outdoor real estate.\n\nThe 21-And-Over Policy\nKeep a physical, government-issued photo ID accessible in your front pocket before approaching the Chrystie Street entrance. Security scans every single guest at street level, as the rooftop strictly enforces a 21+ age limit during evening hours.\n\nThe Sara D. Roosevelt Pivot\nPair your elevated cocktail experience with a ground-level exploration of the surrounding neighborhood. Step right across Chrystie Street before or after your visit to stroll through Sara D. Roosevelt Park and dive into the adjacent Chinatown and Bowery food scenes.\n\nThe Subway Approach\nNavigating to the doorstep via public transit is remarkably quick and direct. Ride the F train straight to the 2nd Avenue station or take the B, D, F, or M train to Broadway-Lafayette Street for an easy three-minute walk to the entrance.",
    "image": "images/138.jpg",
    "cost": null,
    "rating": null,
    "packageId": null,
    "gallery": [],
    "lat": 40.723034,
    "lng": -73.9920355
  },
  {
    "id": "1794677012547",
