    "category": "dining",
    "day": "",
    "website": "https://www.paradiselost.nyc/",
    "address": "Paradise Lost, 100 2nd Ave, New York, NY 10003, United States",
    "summary": "An immersive, high-energy tropical rum bar and subterranean tiki lounge serving elaborate, fiery cocktails in theatrical skull mugs.",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly through the busy East Village grid searching for a subtle entrance. This massive, hyper-themed subterranean tiki oasis is boldly anchored at 100 2nd Avenue, situated prominently near the bustling intersection of East 6th Street.\n\nThe Theatrical Descent\nPrepare for a complete sensory shift the moment you walk through the doors. Leaving the gritty East Village pavement behind, you descend into a heavily stylized, glowing, cavernous space that feels exactly like a shipwrecked, post-apocalyptic tropical island.\n\nThe Elaborate Glassware\nDo not expect standard highball glasses or simple cocktail coupes. The incredibly complex rum concoctions are served in stunning, custom-designed ceramic vessels ranging from massive, glowing tiki idols to highly detailed, smoking shrunken skulls.\n\nThe Signature Ignition\nYou absolutely must order one of their spectacular, large-format flaming cocktails. Watch closely as the expert bartenders execute a brilliant, high-energy theatrical display, showering cinnamon dust over open flames to create massive, crackling sparks right at the bar.\n\nThe Rum Foundation\nEmbrace the deep, incredibly diverse sugarcane spirit menu. The mixologists brilliantly blend multiple high-proof, aged, and botanical rums within a single drink to create deeply complex, layered flavor profiles that perfectly balance sweet, tart, and heavily spiced notes.\n\nThe Themed Provisioning\nDo not skip the highly stylized, tropical food menu. Order a platter of the crispy coconut shrimp or the massive, savory pork sliders to perfectly anchor the high-proof, heavily spirited cocktails during a long, immersive evening in the lounge.\n\nThe Subterranean Aesthetic\nAdmire the incredible, movie-set level of interior detailing throughout the space. The sprawling, dimly lit room is meticulously packed with glowing neon signs, massive tropical foliage, heavy nautical rigging, and brilliantly curated, oddball vintage maritime artifacts.\n\nThe Group Expedition\nBecause the massive, flaming punch bowls are engineered for serious volume, gather a dedicated crew of friends for the visit. Sharing a massive, intricately garnished communal vessel is the absolute best way to experience the high-energy, theatrical nature of the bar.\n\nThe Walk-In Strategy\nIf you do not have a confirmed booking, arrive exactly when the massive wooden doors open early in the evening. Securing a prime stool directly at the main bar provides an incredible, front-row view of the complex, highly choreographed cocktail assembly.\n\nThe Reservation Protocol\nDo not leave a prime weekend evening up to chance in this incredibly popular neighborhood. Book a dedicated table or a sprawling, curved booth well in advance via Resy to guarantee immediate, VIP entry past the bustling, street-level queues.\n\nThe Macro Detail\nBefore taking the first sip of a massive, heavily garnished cocktail, activate your camera’s dedicated macro mode. Get incredibly close to the drink to beautifully capture the intricate, fresh fruit carvings, glowing ice cubes, and the flawless, heavily frosted ceramic mugs.\n\nThe Action Video\nFor a brilliant, cinematic social media clip, use a slow-motion frame rate to flawlessly freeze the exact moment the bartender ignites the flaming lime shell and tosses the crackling, sparking cinnamon dust over the massive, glowing punch bowl.\n\nThe Glow-In-The-Dark Shot\nBecause the subterranean room is dramatically bathed in heavy, colored neon and blacklight, embrace the moody, high-contrast atmosphere. Hold your glowing, brightly colored tropical drink up directly against the vibrant, glowing neon signage for a stunning, stylized portrait.\n\nThe East Village Pivot\nOnce you re-emerge from the heavy, tropical depths, take a beautiful, scenic walk to continue exploring the iconic neighborhood. Head straight down 2nd Avenue to seamlessly transition into the massive, late-night slice shops and bustling dive bars of the surrounding blocks.\n\nThe Subway Approach\nTransit to this subterranean hideaway is incredibly effortless. Take the F train directly to the bustling 2nd Avenue station, or ride the 6 train to Astor Place, emerging from the underground for a brilliant, incredibly short walk straight to the glowing entrance.",
