    "address": "Jhoanes Bakery & Coffee, 33-04 Broadway, Astoria, NY 11106, United States",
    "summary": "A charming, highly celebrated Colombian bakery in Astoria serving flawless pan de bono, rich espresso, and massive savory empanadas.",
    "desc": "The Exact Coordinates\nDo not wander aimlessly along the sprawling blocks of Queens searching for a generic cafe. This charming, highly celebrated Colombian bakery is brilliantly anchored at 33-04 Broadway right in the vibrant heart of Astoria.\n\nThe Free Tasting Hack\nDo not hesitate to politely ask the counter staff if they are offering any complimentary pastry samples for the day. They frequently slice up fresh, brilliant off-menu pound cakes or cookies for guests to flawlessly test before committing to a larger order.\n\nThe Pan de Bono\nYou absolutely must command an order of their legendary, perfectly baked pan de bono. These incredibly soft, flawless Colombian cheese breads perfectly balance a slightly crispy golden exterior with a deeply warm, chewy center.\n\nThe Savory Empanada\nBalance the heavy sugar rush by securing a massive, perfectly fried beef or chicken empanada. The beautifully blistered, golden-yellow cornmeal crust flawlessly locks in the incredibly rich, deeply savory, and heavily seasoned meat filling.\n\nThe Colombian Extraction\nPerfectly cut through the rich, buttery pastries by securing a deeply pulled, highly engineered espresso beverage. The expert baristas brilliantly extract premium, deeply roasted Colombian beans to effortlessly balance the heavy flavor profile of the baked goods.\n\nThe Custom Cake Display\nBefore stepping up to the bustling register, take a moment to admire the brightly lit refrigerated pastry case. The brilliant visual array of incredibly intricate, vibrantly decorated custom cakes provides a stunning preview of the massive culinary craftsmanship waiting inside.\n\nThe Guava Pastry\nIf you crave a brilliant tropical sweetness, secure their highly celebrated guava and cheese pastry. The flawlessly laminated, incredibly flaky dough perfectly encapsulates the brilliant, high-contrast combination of deeply sweet fruit paste and rich, savory cream cheese.\n\nThe Morning Strategy\nPlan your visit perfectly for the early morning hours to guarantee the absolute best selection. Arriving right at opening secures a flawless, still-warm pastry directly from the massive, heavily utilized baking ovens before the commuter rush strikes.\n\nThe Cozy Aesthetic\nAdmire the incredibly warm, beautifully styled interior design the moment you walk through the glass doors. The intimate retail space beautifully utilizes rustic wood accents, brilliant warm lighting, and classic cafe seating that completely defines neighborhood comfort.\n\nThe Window Seat View\nIf you secure a highly coveted table directly against the massive front windows, embrace the Queens urban theater. Watching the relentless, high-speed flow of Broadway traffic and bustling Astoria locals provides a brilliant, highly kinetic backdrop to your coffee.\n\nThe Macro Detail\nActivate your camera's dedicated macro mode exactly when you break open the warm pan de bono. Get incredibly close to beautifully capture the flawless, deeply steaming, and incredibly elastic cheese pull stretching from the golden crust.\n\nThe Crema Capture\nFor a brilliant, cinematic social media video, use a fast shutter speed the exact moment the barista hands over your hot latte. Flawlessly capture the brilliant, heavy microfoam and the perfectly poured, high-contrast latte art settling into the cup.\n\nThe Group Pastry Box\nBecause the baked goods are incredibly dense and beautifully priced, secure a massive, tightly packed pastry box for the road. Hand-selecting an assorted dozen of their traditional Colombian cookies and breads provides a deeply authentic, highly practical souvenir.\n\nThe Moving Image Pivot\nOnce you secure your heavy pastry bags and a fresh, hot coffee, take a highly scenic walk deeper into Astoria. Head seamlessly down the avenue to transition directly into the massive, historically brilliant Museum of the Moving Image for an incredible afternoon.\n\nThe Transit Approach\nNavigating to this bustling Queens corridor is incredibly effortless from anywhere in Manhattan. Simply ride the N or W train directly to the elevated Broadway station, descending the heavy steel stairs for a brilliant, incredibly short walk straight to the glowing storefront.",
